course: dictionary
lesson: 747
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Look for clues: who or what is in the sentence, and what is happening.
explain: A capital letter in the middle of a sentence often means a name. Batman, with a capital B, is a famous comic-book and film superhero who fights crime in Gotham City. In the stories his real name is Bruce Wayne.
explain: With a small b, batman is an old word from the British Army. A batman was a soldier who worked as a personal servant to an officer, so a sentence about polishing boots or carrying kit is about the soldier, not the superhero.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. If the sentence still makes sense with a superhero, it is the name. If it only makes sense with a soldier servant, it is the old word.
fact: A capital letter at the start of a name, such as Batman, shows it is a special name for a person, place or character.
fact: «Batman» (a name) means a famous comic-book and film superhero who fights crime in Gotham City.
fact: In the stories, Batman has no superpowers, but he uses gadgets and training.
fact: «Batman» (old, UK military) means a soldier who worked as a personal servant to an officer.
fact: Films show bats as scary, but real bats are shy, useful animals that eat pests, spread seeds and pollinate flowers.
exercise: «Batman flew over the rooftops of Gotham City to stop the thief.» Who is Batman in this sentence? | *A famous superhero who fights crime | A type of cake | A tall tower in a city | A soldier who served an officer
exercise: «The batman polished the officer's boots and pressed his uniform every morning.» What does batman mean here? | A flying animal that eats insects | A famous superhero | *A soldier who was a personal servant to an officer | A large bag for carrying tools
exercise: Which sentence uses batman as the old military word? | *«The batman cleaned the officer's kit before breakfast.» | «Batman is a name in the comics.» | «Batman has no superpowers, but he is very clever.» | «Batman fights crime in Gotham City.»
test: What is Batman's real name in the stories? | Tom Smith | *Bruce Wayne | Clark Kent | Peter Parker
test: According to the facts about real bats, what do they do? | Wear costumes and fight crime | Fly to Gotham City | *Eat pests, spread seeds and pollinate flowers | Serve officers in the army
exam: Which statement about batman is true? | Batman and batman always mean exactly the same thing | Batman is a word used only in cooking | Batman is a kind of bat that eats fish | *The capitalised Batman is a superhero name, while batman with a small b can be an old military servant
